# Unconditional absolute canonical direct image and native sphere canonical line

The actual direct image of the original threefold canonical section
sheaf is O(-infinity), with O(U)-linear natural equivalences on all opens.
The source is the genuine native alternating-cotangent bundle; the
target is the literal holomorphic vanishing ideal. Both inverse maps
are proved using the actual normalized form, full cusp frame, elliptic
transverse order, and native sheaf gluing.

Separately, the actual Mathlib cotangent Hom bundle of the unchanged
Riemann sphere is holomorphically and fibre-linearly identified with
the square of its original vanishing-ideal bundle. No relative
projection formula or higher-direct-image assertion is presumed here.
